+
+### TUI Slash Command Debugging
+
+Hermes slash commands span Python command registry, TUI gateway bridge, and Ink frontend. Bugs usually come from those layers drifting out of sync.
+
+Key points:
+- Check `COMMAND_REGISTRY` first on the Python side
+- Check TUI command definitions and gateway routing next
+- Diagnose autocomplete, CLI-vs-TUI drift, and live-config-application bugs as cross-layer issues, not isolated frontend bugs
+
+### s6 Container Supervision
+
+For Docker-image service supervision, treat s6-overlay behavior as part of Hermes runtime architecture.
+
+Key points:
+- Distinguish static `s6-rc` services from runtime-registered per-profile gateways
+- Understand the `cont-init.d` boot scripts, profile reconciliation, and CMD-wrapper architecture
+- Debug containerized gateway startup through the supervision tree, not just the gateway CLI
